# BriefingIQ JMeter Runner

Data-population runner (not load testing): Node API + Angular UI execute JMeter plans against BriefingIQ.

## Layout

- `plans/*.jmx` — **active test plans** (primary: `plans/BIQ.jmx`)
- `BIQ.jmx` (repo root) — legacy; do not edit unless explicitly asked
- `server.js` + `jmx-parameters.js` — API, parsing, field-options proxy
- `scripts/validate.js`, `scripts/setup-jmeter-java.js` — prerequisites + JMeter-only Java config
- `ui/` — Angular 21 SPA
- `runs/` — gitignored run artifacts; analyze logs there when debugging runs
- `.jdk/`, `.env` — gitignored local JDK + env overrides (see `.env.example`)

## Dev commands

```bash
npm run init                 # first-time setup
npm run validate             # prerequisite check only
npm run setup:jmeter-java    # detect JDK 11+ → JMETER_JAVA_HOME in .env
npm run install:jmeter-java  # download portable Temurin 17 into .jdk/
npm run install:jmeter-plugins  # copy vendored jpgc-json into JMeter
npm run dev                  # API :5050 + UI :4200
```

## Change discipline

- Minimize scope; match existing patterns in the file you touch
- Do not commit `runs/`, `.env`, `.jdk/`, or Bearer tokens
- Do not create git commits or PRs unless the user asks
- README is the source of truth for prerequisites (Node 20.19+, JMeter 5.4+, jpgc-json in `vendor/jmeter-plugins/`, JMeter Java 11+ / 17+ on Windows)

## Debugging runs

When the user gives a run ID, inspect `runs/<id>__<label>/launcher.log` first (Java command + exit code), then `jmeter.log`, `result.jtl`, and `run.meta.json`.

**Windows JVM crash (`3221225477`):** almost always Java 8 for JMeter — suggest `npm run install:jmeter-java` (keeps system `JAVA_HOME` on Java 8). Confirm fix via `javaHomeSource=JMETER_JAVA_HOME env` in `launcher.log`.
